WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.380
Three nights later the matron of the workhouse where Oliver was born was having tea.

2
00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:10.793
Outside the snow lay frozen in a hard, thick crust and the wind howled sharply.

3
00:00:10.794 --> 00:00:15.610
But everything was warm and cozy inside the room belonging to Mrs. Corney.

4
00:00:15.611 --> 00:00:21.626
The widow sat at a table in front of the cheerful fire and looked around with a self-satisfied air.

5
00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:30.023
"Well," she said to herself. "We all have much to be grateful for, being indoors on a bitter night like this one."

6
00:00:30.024 --> 00:00:35.848
Mrs. Corney had just tasted her first cup of tea when she was disturbed by a rap on her door.

7
00:00:35.849 --> 00:00:46.753
"Come in," said Mrs. Corney sharply. "Some old woman is probably dying. They always die when I'm at meals. What's wrong?"

8
00:00:46.754 --> 00:00:50.086
"Nothing, ma'am, nothing," said a man's voice.

9
00:00:50.087 --> 00:00:57.237
"Dear me!" the matron exclaimed in a much sweeter tone. "Is that Mr. Bumble?"

10
00:00:57.238 --> 00:01:03.912
"At your service, ma'am." The parish officer was carrying his hat in one hand and a bundle in the other.

11
00:01:03.913 --> 00:01:06.420
"Bad weather, Mr. Bumble."

12
00:01:06.421 --> 00:01:15.166
"Bad indeed, ma'am. This very afternoon we gave away twenty loaves of bread and a cheese and a half, and still those paupers are not content."

13
00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:20.824
"Of course not. When would they be?" said the matron, sipping her tea.

14
00:01:20.825 --> 00:01:28.729
"When indeed." Mr. Bumble unpacked his bundle. "I brought the port wine that the board ordered for the infirmary."

15
00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:35.126
He placed the two bottles on top of a chest of drawers and folded up the handkerchief in which they had been wrapped.

16
00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:39.491
He put that in his pocket and picked up his hat as if preparing to go.

17
00:01:39.492 --> 00:01:42.880
"You'll have a very cold walk," said the matron.

18
00:01:42.881 --> 00:01:48.967
"The wind blows sharply tonight, ma'am." Mr. Bumble turned up his coat collar.

19
00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:53.134
"Would you stay and take a cup of tea?" she inquired shyly.

20
00:01:53.135 --> 00:01:57.539
Mr. Bumble instantly turned down his collar and took a seat before the fire.

21
00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:05.110
Mrs. Corney rose to get another cup and saucer. As she sat down, her eyes met Mr. Bumble's, and she blushed.

22
00:02:05.111 --> 00:02:09.285
"Sweet, Mr. Bumble?" she inquired, picking up the sugar.

23
00:02:09.286 --> 00:02:18.023
"Very sweet indeed, ma'am." He regarded her tenderly. As she handed him a cup of tea, he squeezed her little finger.

24
00:02:18.024 --> 00:02:27.435
They talked of Mrs. Corney's cat and kittens. They drank more tea, and Mr. Bumble edged his chair around the table until it touched Mrs. Corney's chair.

25
00:02:27.436 --> 00:02:33.419
The parish officer drank his last drop of tea, ate a piece of toast, and kissed the matron.

26
00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:38.165
"Mr. Bumble!" exclaimed Mrs. Corney in a whisper.

27
00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:45.324
She was so startled that she had quite lost her voice. "Mr. Bumble, I shall scream!"

28
00:02:45.325 --> 00:02:54.975
Mr. Bumble made no reply but put his arm around her waist. Mrs. Corney would have screamed, except just then there was a hasty knocking at the door.

29
00:02:54.976 --> 00:02:59.832
Mr. Bumble darted to the wine bottles and began dusting them with great energy.

30
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:04.316
"Who's there?" Mrs. Corney demanded in her usual sharp voice.

31
00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:11.657
An old pauper woman put her head in at the door. "If you please, mistress, Old Sally is dying."

32
00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:18.554
"Well, what's that to me?" angrily demanded the matron. "I can't keep her alive, can I?"

33
00:03:18.555 --> 00:03:23.062
"No, mistress. She says she has something to tell you."

34
00:03:23.063 --> 00:03:28.546
With much annoyance, Mrs. Corney wrapped herself in a shawl and followed the woman.

35
00:03:28.547 --> 00:03:32.205
Sally was sitting up in bed when they arrived at her bedside.

36
00:03:32.206 --> 00:03:37.451
"You must lie down," said the pauper woman, helping Sally back onto her pillow.

37
00:03:37.452 --> 00:03:44.117
"Send her away," said Old Sally to Mrs. Corney. "Make haste."

38
00:03:44.118 --> 00:03:50.863
Mrs. Corney dismissed the pauper woman. Sally reached out a hand and pulled her down into a chair.

39
00:03:50.864 --> 00:04:06.339
"Now listen to me," said the dying woman. "In this very room I once nursed a pretty young creature. She gave birth to a boy and died. Let me think . . . what was the year?"

40
00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.180
"Never mind the year. What about her?"

41
00:04:10.181 --> 00:04:26.077
"She was barely dead when I stole it. The only thing she had. A necklace. Gold. Pure gold. She could have sold it for food or clothing, but she kept it safe around her neck."

42
00:04:26.078 --> 00:04:30.997
"Gold!" Mrs. Corney bent eagerly over the dying woman.

43
00:04:30.998 --> 00:04:34.498
"Go on. What happened to it?"

44
00:04:34.523 --> 00:04:36.732
"And the boy . . ."

45
00:04:36.756 --> 00:04:38.561
"What boy?"

46
00:04:38.561 --> 00:04:49.314
"They named him Oliver. He grew to look so like his mother. Poor girl. I always thought of her whenever I saw him."

47
00:04:49.315 --> 00:04:53.735
"But the necklace. What did you do with the necklace?"

48
00:04:53.736 --> 00:05:02.981
Sally pulled the matron closer and whispered something. Then she closed her eyes and died. Mrs. Corney quickly left the room.

49
00:05:02.982 --> 00:05:08.711
"She had nothing to tell me after all," Mrs. Corney said to the pauper woman, who was waiting in the hall.

50
00:05:08.712 --> 00:05:12.957
Meanwhile Mr. Bumble had been left by himself in Mrs. Corney's room.

51
00:05:12.958 --> 00:05:21.298
He opened the closet, counted the teaspoons, weighed the sugar tongs in his hand, and inspected a milk pot to be sure it was genuine silver.

52
00:05:21.299 --> 00:05:27.711
Trying to decide how much she was worth, he then sat down to take an inventory of the furniture.

53
00:05:27.712 --> 00:05:34.774
Still Mrs. Corney did not return. He recounted the teaspoons and double-checked the condition of the furniture.

54
00:05:34.775 --> 00:05:40.274
Perhaps, he thought, he should have a quick glance through the contents of Mrs. Corney's chest of drawers.

55
00:05:40.275 --> 00:05:47.195
Mr. Bumble listened at the keyhole to make sure no one was coming. Then he opened the three long drawers.

56
00:05:47.196 --> 00:05:52.853
Among the various garments of good fashion and texture, he found a small padlocked box.

57
00:05:52.854 --> 00:05:58.417
Mr. Bumble shook the box and it gave forth a pleasant sound like the clinking of coins.

58
00:05:58.418 --> 00:06:05.171
Mr. Bumble returned with a stately walk to the fireplace. "I'll do it!" he declared to himself.

59
00:06:05.172 --> 00:06:09.417
Just then Mrs. Corney burst into the room in a state of agitation.

60
00:06:09.418 --> 00:06:12.750
"What's wrong?" asked the parish officer in alarm.

61
00:06:12.751 --> 00:06:20.068
"Oh, nothing, nothing," she said breathlessly. "Tea! I must have more tea."

62
00:06:20.069 --> 00:06:30.909
Mr. Bumble bustled about, making another pot of tea. He watched with concern as Mrs. Corney drank the hot liquid. The tea had a settling effect upon her.

63
00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.105
"You know the master of the workhouse is dying, my dear?" he said.

64
00:06:35.129 --> 00:06:36.720
"Yes."

65
00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:45.632
"He may not live another week, and his death will open up a vacancy that perhaps I might fill." Mr. Bumble suddenly grasped her hands.

66
00:06:45.633 --> 00:06:54.946
"Oh, Mrs. Corney, what a prospect this opens! What an opportunity for a joining of our hearts! Will you say yes to me?"

67
00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.625
"Yes!"

68
00:06:56.625 --> 00:07:03.126
And with that the happy couple was engaged to be married. But Mr. Bumble had one more question.

69
00:07:03.127 --> 00:07:05.951
"What was it that agitated you so?"

70
00:07:05.952 --> 00:07:14.833
"Nothing in particular," Mrs. Corney said evasively. "I'll tell you sometime after we're married, dear."

